INT. STARLIGHT ROLLER RINK - NIGHT

Disco ball. Carpeted walls. A faded sign: LAST SKATE. The speakers play a slow song nobody asked for.

TARIQ OKAFOR-LANE, 17, rental skates two sizes too big, clings to the rail. JOSEFINA "JOJO" VARGAS, 17, graceful on her own wheels, skates backward in front of him. MR. LINDQVIST, 60s, owner, apron over a windbreaker, stacks plastic baskets at the snack counter, listening.

JOJO
You're doing it wrong.

TARIQ
I'm doing it.

JOJO
You're clutching.

TARIQ
It's called balance.

JOJO
It's called terror.

He lets go. Windmills. Grabs the rail again. Jojo laughs and sails away, spins, comes back.

JOJO (CONT'D)
Come on, Tariq. Last night in the building. Let me see you skate.

TARIQ
It's closing?

JOJO
Mr. Lindqvist sold it. Condos.

Tariq glances at the counter. Mr. Lindqvist is wiping a spotless surface.

TARIQ
Why didn't you say?

JOJO
I'm saying.

TARIQ
I mean before.

JOJO
Before, you weren't talking to me.

TARIQ
You weren't talking to me.

They look at each other. Disco light slides across their faces.

TARIQ (CONT'D)
I'm sorry, Jo.

JOJO
For what?

TARIQ
For what I said in the cafeteria.

JOJO
Which part?

TARIQ
All of it.

She skates to him. Holds out both hands.

JOJO
Come on. Let go of the wall.

He lets go. Takes her hands. She backs away slowly, pulling him across the floor. He wobbles. Straightens.

TARIQ
I'm doing it.

JOJO
You're doing it.

They circle. Behind them the song fades into a different song. Mr. Lindqvist dims the lights another notch.

MR. LINDQVIST (O.S.)
(calling from the counter)
Five more minutes, you two.

JOJO
(calling back)
Ten, Mr. L!

MR. LINDQVIST (O.S.)
Five!

Tariq grins. For a lap, his skating looks almost natural.

TARIQ
Where will you go? After?

JOJO
There's a rink in Eastbrook.

TARIQ
That's forty minutes.

JOJO
I've got a bike.

TARIQ
I haven't.

JOJO
Then borrow one.

Tariq nods. The ball spins. They skate in silence for a long time.

JOJO (CONT'D)
My dad's moving us in June.

TARIQ
Where?

JOJO
Tucson.

He stumbles. She catches him.

TARIQ
You were going to tell me?

JOJO
I'm telling you.

TARIQ
Same as the rink.

JOJO
Same as the rink.

He steadies himself. They keep circling. The song ends.

The overhead lights flicker once, twice. Mr. Lindqvist's silhouette stands at the switch.

MR. LINDQVIST (O.S.)
That's it, kids.

Tariq doesn't let go of her hand.

TARIQ
One more lap.

JOJO
Mr. L!

MR. LINDQVIST (O.S.)
(a long beat)
One more lap.

He kills the music. In the silence there is only the soft rumble of two sets of wheels on old boards, going round and round.
